### Campaign Engine — request collection
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, JetBrains HTTP client and Visual Studio.
### Start the API with `dotnet run --project src/CampaignEngine.Api` (Development keys below).

@base = http://localhost:5080/api/v1
@admin = dev-admin-key
@pos = dev-pos-key

### 1. A global "never discount" list (tobacco, gold, gift cards …)
POST {{base}}/product-lists
X-Api-Key: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "REGULATED",
  "name": "Products that may never be discounted",
  "kind": "globalExclusion",
  "skus": ["TOBACCO-001", "GOLD-22K-5G", "GIFTCARD-100"]
}

### 2. Bulk import SKUs from a CSV export of the ERP (first column = SKU)
PUT {{base}}/product-lists/REGULATED/skus/import?mode=append
X-Api-Key: {{admin}}
Content-Type: text/csv

sku,description
TOBACCO-002,Cigarettes
TOBACCO-003,Cigars

### 3. "3 for 2 on t-shirts" in stores and online on weekends
# @name create
POST {{base}}/campaigns
X-Api-Key: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SS26-TSHIRT-3X2",
  "name": "T-shirts: 3 for 2",
  "priority": 100,
  "channels": ["store", "web"],
  "schedule": {
    "startsAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00+03:00",
    "endsAt": "2026-09-01T00:00:00+03:00",
    "timeZone": "Europe/Istanbul",
    "daysOfWeek": ["saturday", "sunday"]
  },
  "target": { "categories": ["apparel-tshirt"] },
  "reward": { "type": "buyXGetY", "buyQuantity": 2, "getQuantity": 1 },
  "limits": { "maxDiscountPerOrder": 1000 },
  "displayMessage": "3 for 2 on all t-shirts",
  "metadata": { "erpCampaignNo": "2026-0042" }
}

### 4. Check it against live campaigns before going live
POST {{base}}/campaigns/conflicts
X-Api-Key: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "WEB-TSHIRT-40",
  "name": "Web: 40% on t-shirts",
  "channels": ["web"],
  "target": { "categories": ["apparel-tshirt"] },
  "reward": { "type": "percentageDiscount", "percent": 40 }
}

### 5. Activate (409 if an error-level conflict exists; add ?force=true to override)
POST {{base}}/campaigns/{{create.response.body.id}}/activate
X-Api-Key: {{admin}}

### 6. Price a basket (POS / web). explain=true tells why other campaigns did not apply.
POST {{base}}/evaluate?explain=true
X-Api-Key: {{pos}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "store",
  "storeId": "IST-001",
  "timestamp": "2026-06-06T11:00:00+03:00",
  "customer": { "id": "C-1001", "segments": ["gold"] },
  "lines": [
    { "lineId": "1", "sku": "TS-001-M", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 299.90, "categories": ["apparel", "apparel-tshirt"] },
    { "lineId": "2", "sku": "TS-002-L", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 199.90, "categories": ["apparel", "apparel-tshirt"] },
    { "lineId": "3", "sku": "TOBACCO-001", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 95.00 }
  ],
  "payment": { "method": "creditCard", "cardBin": "45436012", "installments": 3 }
}

### 7. Confirm the sale (idempotent on transactionId)
POST {{base}}/redemptions
X-Api-Key: {{pos}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "IST-001-20260606-000123",
  "cart": {
    "channel": "store",
    "storeId": "IST-001",
    "timestamp": "2026-06-06T11:00:00+03:00",
    "lines": [
      { "lineId": "1", "sku": "TS-001-M", "quantity": 3, "unitPrice": 299.90, "categories": ["apparel-tshirt"] }
    ]
  }
}

### 8. Customer returned everything
POST {{base}}/redemptions/IST-001-20260606-000123/reverse
X-Api-Key: {{pos}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "full return" }

### 9. Snapshot for local evaluation (repeat with If-None-Match: <ETag> → 304)
GET {{base}}/snapshot
X-Api-Key: {{pos}}

### 10. Get notified about changes
POST {{base}}/webhooks
X-Api-Key: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "https://pos-sync.example.com/campaign-hook", "events": ["campaign.*", "productList.*"] }
